module embedded::wdt;

// Watchdog control. Startup code disables every hardware watchdog it knows
// about before `start()` runs; nothing else in the library touches a watchdog.
// Applications that want watchdog protection call `feed()` from their main
// loop after enabling the watchdog with MCU-specific code.

// Disable all watchdogs that can reset the MCU. Safe to call more than once.
fn void disable();

// Reset the watchdog timeout. A no-op when every watchdog is disabled.
fn void feed();
